rsa-prime-range: validate that both RSA primes are in the acceptable range

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 1, "RSA", "Introduction"): "When
loading an RSA key, the TPM validates that its public and private portions
are properly paired by dividing the public modulus by the single private prime
and requiring that the remainder be zero. ... The TPM will also validate that
the provided and computed prime factors are in an acceptable range. To be
acceptable, the square of the prime is required to have the same number of
significant bits as the public modulus." (also Part 2, TPM2B_PRIVATE_KEY_RSA:
"All primes are required to have exactly half the number of significant bits
as the public modulus, and the square of each prime is required to have the
same number of significant bits as the public modulus.")

The reference only checks that the provided prime has half the size of the
modulus with its most significant bit SET (CryptoCommon_ValidateKeys()); the
computed prime Q = N / P is not checked at all. A key whose Q has one bit more
than half the modulus is therefore accepted, and under a fixedTPM parent its
CRT form gets a prime size larger than half the modulus (RSA-1024: a 325-byte
sensitive value that TPM2_Load then rejects; RSA-2048: PackExponent() exceeds
RSA_MAX_PRIME and the TPM enters failure mode). CryptRsaLoadPrivateExponent()
now checks both primes after the division and returns TPM_RC_BINDING (its
code for a key whose parts do not fit together), as tpm-rs does.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/crypt/CryptRsa.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/crypt/CryptRsa.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/crypt/CryptRsa.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/crypt/CryptRsa.c
@@ -955,6 +955,17 @@ CryptRsaLoadPrivateExponent(TPMT_PUBLIC* publicArea, TPMT_SENSITIVE* sensitive)
             // some intermediate step.
             GOTO_ERROR_UNLESS(ExtMath_Divide(Z->Q, bnQr, bnN, Z->P));
             GOTO_ERROR_UNLESS(ExtMath_IsZero(bnQr));
+            // tpm-rs differential testing (bug fix): both primes must be in the
+            // acceptable range (Part 1: "the square of the prime is required to
+            // have the same number of significant bits as the public modulus").
+            {
+                CRYPT_INT_VAR(bnSquare, MAX_RSA_KEY_BITS * 2);
+                int nBits = ExtMath_MostSigBitNum(bnN);
+                GOTO_ERROR_UNLESS(ExtMath_Multiply(bnSquare, Z->P, Z->P));
+                GOTO_ERROR_UNLESS(ExtMath_MostSigBitNum(bnSquare) == nBits);
+                GOTO_ERROR_UNLESS(ExtMath_Multiply(bnSquare, Z->Q, Z->Q));
+                GOTO_ERROR_UNLESS(ExtMath_MostSigBitNum(bnSquare) == nBits);
+            }
             // Compute the private exponent and return it if found
             GOTO_ERROR_UNLESS(ComputePrivateExponent(bnE, Z));
             GOTO_ERROR_UNLESS(PackExponent(&sensitive->sensitive.rsa, Z));
